# Stack

- Expo Development Builds (not Expo Go)
- React Native
- TypeScript (strict)
- Zustand
- expo-sqlite
- NativeWind
- Expo Router — satisfies the React Navigation requirement, since Expo Router is built on
  React Navigation (ADR-01)

Android and iOS only. Web is not a target.

Dependencies are installed per milestone, not up front. See the milestone table in
`docs/roadmap.md`.

# Folder Structure

Application source lives under `src/`; native module source lives under `modules/`.

- src/app — Expo Router routes
- src/components/ui
- src/features
- src/hooks
- src/native
- src/repositories
- src/services
- src/store
- src/theme
- src/types
- src/utils
- modules/snoozepulse-audio — Swift + Kotlin

# Layering

```text
UI → Store → Services → Repositories → SQLite / Native
```

The store never calls a repository directly. Services hold business logic; repositories hold
SQL. They never merge.

# Principles

- Use theme tokens. Sample new color values from the design images; never invent them.
- Depend on interfaces; never `new` a concrete class in a store, hook, or component.
- Use functional components.
- Avoid `any`.
- Keep components small and composable.
